1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,940
What I've learned from my social media activity is that it doesn't always have to be the most extreme thing to create a viral video.

2
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:20,100
The most viral video on my channel is a jump where a friend of mine simply flies away from the cliff in a completely normal way.

3
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:27,200
It got 56 million views. I'm standing at the exit, filming it with my iPhone.

4
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:43,200
So it simply isn't true that only those stunts attract the most attention, although major stunts naturally generate a lot of attention.

5
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:55,200
It can lead to a spiral where you also allow yourself to be motivated by that.

6
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:05,780
Personally, there was also a time when I was much more active on social media and pursued it much more actively.

7
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:11,720
By now, my view counts are actually relatively unimportant to me.

8
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:18,280
I post whatever I feel like posting and don't really let myself be guided by the numbers.

9
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:25,680
Even so, as the camera flyer I am, I'm very stoked when I have a beautiful video.
